1.0.1 2026-10-16 (NEMAR)
  - Added sub-32/eeg/sub-32_task-oddball_eeg.json and _channels.tsv, missing since the source release
    (OpenNeuro ds003620 has none for sub-32). Task-level values are those shared by all 43 other
    subjects; RecordingDuration = DataPoints x SamplingInterval of its .vhdr (3858.798 s).
    DeviceSerialNumber is not set (not recorded for this file).
  - channels.tsv of every subject (identical in all 43): column sampling_reference renamed to
    sampling_frequency (BIDS); reference column holds the EEGReference FCz instead of 'common';
    x_dir/y_dir/z_dir typed MISC with units mg, as stated in every .vhdr header (were EEG, uV);
    the uV unit written in UTF-8 (was a Latin-1 byte); LF line endings.
  - eeg.json of every subject: key MiscChannelCount (not a BIDS key) renamed to MISCChannelCount.
  - Each subject's _electrodes.json held coordinate-system keys (EEGCoordinateSystem RAS, mm), not
    column descriptions: moved unchanged to sub-XX/eeg/sub-XX_coordsystem.json (BIDS requires it with
    electrodes.tsv). Identical in all 44 subjects. EEGCoordinateSystem "RAS" (not a BIDS
    keyword) written "Other"; the existing EEGCoordinateSystemDescription defines it (RAS, mm).
  - participants.tsv: participant_id written as the subject folders (sub-01, was sub-1); trailing empty
    row removed. Privacy: the DOB column (exact date of birth) is removed and study_date is reduced to the
    year (YYYY), because no consent or authorization covering publication of the exact dates is documented;
    age (years) is kept as released. participants.json updated.
  - electrodes.tsv impedance 'not' (sub-01 4 rows, sub-18 12, sub-25 32) written n/a.
  - Not fixable here: sub-31 has no _eeg.eeg data file, in the source release as well.
